 # Decisions
 
 No spec gaps identified before implementation. The issue explicitly requires a canonical/packaged AGENTS pointer to `using-forge`, preservation of user content and harness behavior, and no duplicated dynamic output. Forbidden shared files will remain untouched.
+
+## 2026-08-01 — Shepherd release-gate recovery
+
+Exact-head shipping exposed a permanent false `BLOCKED-THREADS` projection: post-push automation/completion comments were counted as actionable while their adapter IDs were omitted from evidence. After that was removed, Qodo's in-place exact-head review refresh remained falsely stale because the adapter discarded `updatedAt`.
+
+The narrow recovery stays fail-closed:
+- unknown bot comments and CodeRabbit finding comments remain actionable;
+- actor identity alone never suppresses a direct comment; only bounded, recognized status/lifecycle body envelopes are non-actionable;
+- known GitHub Actions package-size, exact Actions-run review-trigger, refreshed-success, and Forge-monitor bodies are informational only when their complete envelope matches and no explicit finding is appended;
+- CodeRabbit's explicit `Review finished` command envelope and its full-exact-head `No actionable comments` summary require complete provider framing and no contradictory finding marker;
+- Qodo's clean refresh requires complete provider framing, zero active counts, a generated full-exact-head commit URL, a known footer, and no unresolved provider-native finding summary; struck-and-resolved historical details remain allowed;
+- stale-head CodeRabbit/Qodo summaries remain actionable;
+- blocker evidence accepts the adapter's stable `id` shape;
+- comment freshness consistently uses the later valid `createdAt` / `updatedAt`, so in-place finding/status edits cannot disappear;
+- an older bot Review is superseded only by the same Qodo bot's explicit zero-bug/zero-rule-violation summary, updated after the head push and containing the full exact head SHA;
+- exact-SHA finding text, wrong-bot summaries, abbreviated SHAs, and pre-push summaries remain blocked;
+- comment updates extend the ten-minute settle window.
+
+This ship-blocking gate fix remains in #471 because deleting bot comments or bypassing `forge merge --auto` would violate the release policy.
+
+Independent review of local SHA `5012d028` invalidated its pending approval before push by reproducing false-clean cases in the initial predicates. The repair is intentionally one convergence amendment: RED provider/automation mutations, production hardening, live-shape compatibility, focused aggregate, then a fresh exact-SHA review wave. No prior exact-SHA approval survives that amendment.
+
+## 2026-08-01 — Final false-clean boundary
+
+Exact-SHA review of `cdabb072` proved that bounded framing was still too permissive: success substrings and header/footer checks allowed arbitrary middle text; malformed timestamps, missing bot-review commit identity, and absent GraphQL connections could disappear; exact push-time equality was treated as stale; and `login`/`login[bot]` aliases bypassed latest-per-author dedupe.
+
+The final convergence amendment therefore applies these invariants:
+- every recognized multi-line provider envelope consumes the complete ordered line grammar; unknown, extra, duplicate, or contradictory lines remain actionable;
+- the Forge monitor's complete renderer grammar is informational for every verdict, preventing its sticky comment from feeding back into and permanently locking its own verdict;
+- malformed GraphQL connections and missing actor identities throw into `safeRead` and become explicit unreadable/degraded evidence rather than empty collections;
+- bot aliases canonicalize before latest-review dedupe;
+- missing/invalid comment timestamps, review timestamps, or full bot-review commit OIDs force `UNKNOWN`, retaining stable IDs in evidence where records reached the verdict core;
+- actionable comment activity exactly equal to the recorded push time blocks conservatively; clean lifecycle refreshes still require strictly post-push activity before superseding stale review evidence.
+
+The live patched verdict remains diagnostic only. It cannot authorize push or merge, and every amendment invalidates earlier exact-SHA review.
